@startuml Client Authentication Flow

!theme plain
title JWT Authentication Flow for Client

actor User
participant Client
participant "OAuth Provider\n(Google/Kakao/Naver)" as OAuth
participant "Auth API" as Auth
participant "Protected API" as API

== 1. OAuth Login ==
User -> Client: Click login button
Client -> OAuth: Redirect to OAuth login\n(e.g., Google OAuth URL)
OAuth -> User: Show login form
User -> OAuth: Enter credentials
OAuth -> Client: Redirect with authorization code\n(callback URL)

Client -> Auth: POST /api/auth/oauth2/authenticate\nAuthorization: Bearer {authorizationCode}
note right: Include provider info (google/kakao/naver)
Auth -> OAuth: Verify authorization code
OAuth --> Auth: User info
Auth --> Client: 200 OK\n{accessToken, refreshToken}
note right: Store both tokens securely

== 2. API Calls ==
Client -> API: GET /api/resource\nAuthorization: Bearer {accessToken}
API --> Client: 200 OK\n{resource data}

== 3. Token Refresh (when access token expires) ==
Client -> API: GET /api/resource\nAuthorization: Bearer {expiredToken}
API --> Client: 401 Unauthorized

Client -> Auth: POST /api/auth/refresh\n{refreshToken}
Auth --> Client: 200 OK\n{newAccessToken, newRefreshToken}
note right: Replace old tokens with new ones

Client -> API: GET /api/resource\nAuthorization: Bearer {newAccessToken}
API --> Client: 200 OK\n{resource data}

== 4. Logout ==
Client -> Auth: POST /api/auth/logout
Auth --> Client: 200 OK
note right: Clear stored tokens

@enduml